      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the dimensions of Mateen's rectangular backyard and then calculate its area. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we know that walking the length 25 times means the distance walked is \\( 25 \\times l \\) meters, which is given as 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 25l = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( l \\), we get:\n\\[ l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNext, we know that walking the perimeter 10 times means the distance walked is \\( 10 \\times 2(l + w) \\) meters, which is also given as 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 10 \\times 2(l + w) = 1000 \\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[ 20(l + w) = 1000 \\]\nDividing both sides by 20, we get:\n\\[ l + w = 50 \\]\n\nNow we have a system of two equations:\n1. \\( l = 40 \\)\n2. \\( l + w = 50 \\)\n\nSubstituting \\( l = 40 \\) into the second equation, we get:\n\\[ 40 + w = 50 \\]\nSolving for \\( w \\), we get:\n\\[ w = 50 - 40 = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNow that we have the length and the width of the backyard, we can calculate its area. The area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by the formula:\n\\[ A = l \\times w \\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( l \\) and \\( w \\), we get:\n\\[ A = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\).",
