      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve for the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the rectangular backyard first. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nAccording to the problem, walking the length 25 times will cover 1000 meters:\n\\[ 25l = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( l \\):\n\\[ l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNext, we know that walking the perimeter 10 times will also cover 1000 meters:\n\\[ 10 \\times 2(l + w) = 1000 \\]\nSimplifying this equation:\n\\[ 2(l + w) = 100 \\]\n\\[ l + w = 50 \\]\n\nNow we have two equations:\n1. \\( l = 40 \\)\n2. \\( l + w = 50 \\)\n\nSubstituting \\( l = 40 \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 40 + w = 50 \\]\n\\[ w = 10 \\]\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of the rectangle is given by:\n\\[ A = l \\times w \\]\n\\[ A = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{400}\n\\]",
